  "id": "process-dissociation-procedure",
  "term": "process-dissociation procedure",
  "definition": "The process-dissociation procedure is a method used to separate the influence of different mental processes that contribute to performance on a task. In this context, it is used to distinguish short-term memory for the items themselves from memory for the order in which they were presented.",
